<title>SPAIN: Bank of Spain cuts key rate to 5.50 pct from 5.75.</title>
<headline>Bank of Spain cuts key rate to 5.50 pct from 5.75.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain said it cut its key money rate to 5.50 percent from 5.75 percent at today's regular repurchase tender for central bank certificates.</p>
<p>It allotted 2.38 trillion pesetas against 2.43 trillion bid.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
